<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">mount</ansi>

Your company can keep one mount, which adds to how much you can carry
and eases the walk for the company members riding it.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What a mount does</ansi>

A mount adds to your company's cargo capacity (<ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>). It also
carries riders: the leader first, then companions in order, up to
however many the mount takes. A rider strains less with every step they
walk beside you (<ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>); a route travelled together goes a
little faster too. Anyone not riding, or not currently with you, gets
none of this.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">mount</ansi>
  Shows your current mount, if any, and its cargo-capacity bonus.

  <ansi fg="command">mount stable [type]</ansi>
  Assigns your company a mount of that type, replacing any mount you
  already had.

  <ansi fg="command">mount release</ansi>
  Gives up your current mount.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help travel</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>.
